        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Kluge, Sidney Salkow\n- Works: Yesterday Girl\n- Roles: author, philosopher, academic, film director, screenwriter, television director\n- Topics: New German Cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Salkow was born on June 16, 1911, and he was an American film director, screenwriter, and television director.\n- Alexander Kluge was born on February 14, 1932, and he is a German author, philosopher, academic, and film director.\n- Yesterday Girl, also titled Abschied von gestern and translated as \"Farewell to Yesterday,\" is a 1966 New German Cinema film written and directed by Alexander Kluge.\n- Sidney Salkow directed more than 50 motion pictures and died on October 18, 2000.",
